---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";

const rows = [
  { issue: "Team Conflict",          assume: "15 cases/yr",        cur: "$70,500",  orch: "$35,250", save: "$35,250" },
  { issue: "Absenteeism",            assume: "10 employees (10%)", cur: "$25,000",  orch: "$12,500", save: "$12,500" },
  { issue: "Underperformance",       assume: "5 cases/yr",         cur: "$47,500",  orch: "$23,750", save: "$23,750" },
  { issue: "Headhunter Fees",        assume: "10 hires/yr",        cur: "$140,000", orch: "$56,000", save: "$84,000" },
  { issue: "Bad Hires, Realized",    assume: "24% of 10 hires/yr", cur: "$67,200",  orch: "$26,900", save: "$40,300" },
  { issue: "Termination Gone Wrong", assume: "1 case/yr",          cur: "$65,000",  orch: "$19,500", save: "$45,500" },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Pitch | Orchestral HR Consulting"
  description="What reactive people practices actually cost, and what changes when issues get caught early instead of managed in crisis."
  current="pitch"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">The Pitch</span>
      <h1>Orchestral helps with fine tuning to drive people performance.</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="staff" role="presentation"><span>&#9834;</span></div>

  <section class="section section--flush" id="proactive">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <span class="section-num section-num--glyph">&#9834;</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">Proactive People Practices vs. Reactive</h2>
        <p class="section-dek">
          People issues are cost effective to resolve while they&rsquo;re still a single note out of
          place, and before they turn into full discord. Here&rsquo;s what waiting on this costs, and
          how staying in tune protects your bottom line.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="stat-grid stagger">
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="v count-up">~$40,000</span>
          <span class="k">A year of leadership capacity lost when a leader spends 20% of their time off-script on people issues.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="v count-up">$460,200</span>
          <span class="k">Annual cost of 15% turnover in a 100-employee business, at $30,680 per turnover event.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="v count-up">$394,700</span>
          <span class="k">Potential annual savings with people issues caught early instead of managed in crisis.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="numbers">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <span class="section-num section-num--glyph">&#9835;</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">Fine-Tuning the Numbers</h2>
        <p class="section-dek">
          A leader spending 20% of their time (up to a full day a week) off-script on people issues
          instead of focusing on driving revenue and production, that&rsquo;s roughly $40,000 a year of
          leadership capacity spent troubleshooting instead of conducting the business forward.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="business-case">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <span class="section-num section-num--glyph">&#9834;</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">The Business Case: 100 Employees, 15% Turnover</h2>
        <p class="section-dek">
          Here are the costs, and what changes when turnover drops 5 pts. to 10% with issues
          getting caught early instead of managed in crisis.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="callout reveal" style="margin-top:0;">
        <span class="k">At 15% turnover, that&rsquo;s</span>
        <span class="v count-up">~$460,200 a year</span>
        <p>
          15 replacements &times; $30,680 average cost per turnover event. Drop turnover 5 points to 10%,
          and you save ~$153,400/year.*
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="where-cost-hides">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <span class="section-num section-num--glyph">&#9837;</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">Where People Cost Hides: Annual Impact</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="table-wrap reveal">
        <table class="figures">
          <caption class="sr-only">
            Annual cost of people issues at 15% turnover compared with Orchestral support, and the resulting savings.
          </caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Issue</th>
              <th scope="col">Assumption</th>
              <th scope="col" class="num">Current &mdash; 15% turnover</th>
              <th scope="col" class="num">With Orchestral</th>
              <th scope="col" class="num">Savings</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="stagger">
            {rows.map((r) => (
              <tr>
                <td class="issue"><span class="note">&#9837;</span>{r.issue}</td>
                <td>{r.assume}</td>
                <td class="num">{r.cur}</td>
                <td class="num">{r.orch}</td>
                <td class="num save">{r.save}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
          <tfoot>
            <tr>
              <td>Total</td>
              <td></td>
              <td class="num">$415,200</td>
              <td class="num">$173,900</td>
              <td class="num save">$241,300</td>
            </tr>
          </tfoot>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="callout callout--total reveal">
        <p class="callout-lead">
          Add the $153,400 saved by reducing turnover plus the above giving your business a potential
        </p>
        <span class="k">Grand total of savings</span>
        <span class="v count-up">$394,700 / annually</span>
      </div>

      <p class="footnote">
        *Illustrative business case for a hypothetical 100-employee company with a blended average salary
        of $70,000 along with a leader compensation of $200k. &ldquo;Current&rdquo; reflects a 15% annual
        turnover rate; &ldquo;With Orchestral&rdquo; reflects turnover reduced to 10% (10 replacements per
        year). Headhunter-fee and bad-hire figures are calculated at the 10-hires/year volume.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand />
</BaseLayout>
